<!DOCTYPE html>
<html class="brand-color-background antialiased" lang="en" data-theme="light" style="font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

    <!-- Primary Meta Tags -->
    <title>AI Fantasy Premier League Picks, Every Gameweek - Coffee & Fun LLC</title>
    <meta name="title" content="AI Fantasy Premier League Picks, Every Gameweek - Coffee & Fun LLC" />
    <meta name="description" content="An AI picks a Fantasy Premier League squad, starting eleven and captain every gameweek of 2026/27, with the reasoning published before each deadline. Free league, code bsg8nz." />
    <meta name="author" content="Coffee & Fun LLC" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />

    <!-- Canonical URL -->
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.coffeeandfun.com/fpl/" />

    <!-- Favicon -->
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/images/brand/favicon.png" sizes="any" />

    <!-- Open Graph -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Coffee & Fun" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="AI Fantasy Premier League Picks, Every Gameweek - Coffee & Fun LLC" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="An AI picks a Fantasy Premier League squad, starting eleven and captain every gameweek of 2026/27, with the reasoning published before each deadline. Free league, code bsg8nz." />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://www.coffeeandfun.com/fpl/" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://www.coffeeandfun.com/assets/images/social/pages/fpl.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Can you beat our AI in Fantasy Premier League? Join our league, code BSG8NZ" />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_US" />

    <!-- Twitter Card -->
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:site" content="@bycoffeeandfun" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="AI Fantasy Premier League Picks, Every Gameweek - Coffee & Fun LLC" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="An AI picks a Fantasy Premier League squad, starting eleven and captain every gameweek of 2026/27, with the reasoning published before each deadline." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.coffeeandfun.com/assets/images/social/pages/fpl.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="Can you beat our AI in Fantasy Premier League? Join our league, code BSG8NZ" />

    <meta name="theme-color" content="#fef5ec" />

    <!-- Structured Data.
         Deliberately WebPage and not WebApplication: the weekly picks tool does not
         exist yet, and marking up software that does not run is exactly the kind of
         thing that earns a structured data manual action. Upgrade this node to
         WebApplication when the live XI ships. -->
    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@graph": [
          {
            "@type": "WebPage",
            "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/fpl/#webpage",
            "url": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/fpl/",
            "name": "AI Fantasy Premier League Picks, Every Gameweek",
            "description": "An AI picks a Fantasy Premier League squad, starting eleven and captain every gameweek of the 2026/27 season, with the reasoning published before each deadline.",
            "inLanguage": "en",
            "isPartOf": { "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/#website" },
            "publisher": { "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/#organization" },
            "primaryImageOfPage": {
              "@type": "ImageObject",
              "url": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/assets/images/social/pages/fpl.png",
              "width": 1200,
              "height": 630
            },
            "significantLink": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/blog/ai-fantasy-premier-league-experiment/"
          },
          {
            "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
            "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/fpl/#breadcrumb",
            "itemListElement": [
              {
                "@type": "ListItem",
                "position": 1,
                "name": "Home",
                "item": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/"
              },
              {
                "@type": "ListItem",
                "position": 2,
                "name": "AI Fantasy Premier League Picks",
                "item": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/fpl/"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "@type": "FAQPage",
            "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/fpl/#faq",
            "mainEntity": [
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "When do the picks go live?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "The first squad is published before the opening deadline of the 2026/27 Premier League season, which is Friday 21 August 2026 at 18:30 BST, ahead of Arsenal against Coventry that evening. After that a new set of picks and the reasoning behind them goes up every gameweek."
                }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Is the league free to join?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "Yes. Algorithm By Coffee & Fun LLC is a free invitational classic league with no entry fee and no prizes. Charging entry for a competition raises gambling and prize competition law questions, so it was ruled out deliberately."
                }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Can I join after the season has started?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "Yes. Fantasy Premier League classic leagues can be joined at any point in the season. Your score in the league counts from the gameweek you join onward, so joining late means fewer points to compete with."
                }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "What data does the AI use to pick the team?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "Free public data only. The official FPL API for scoring, minutes, prices, ownership, Opta expected goals and injury status, with Vaastav's historical dataset for earlier seasons. Understat for player-level expected goals across the big five European leagues. Football-Data.co.uk for results, odds history and referees. ClubElo for team strength and Open-Meteo for weather. Transfermarkt, FBref, Fantasy Football Scout, Fantasy Football Hub and FootyStats are deliberately not used, because the first two restrict automated access and the rest are subscriptions."
                }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Will the bad weeks be published too?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "Yes. Every gameweek gets written up the same way whether it went well or badly, with no retroactive edits. Publishing only the good weeks would make the whole experiment worthless."
                }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Is this betting advice?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "No. This is a free fantasy football experiment run for fun by one person. Nothing here is betting advice and no money changes hands at any point."
                }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Is this affiliated with the Premier League?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "No. This is an independent project by Coffee & Fun LLC and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to the Premier League or the official Fantasy Premier League game."
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    </script>

    {% include schema-org.liquid %}

    {% bundledCss %}
    {% pageCss "fpl" %}
    {% include sketch-styles.liquid %}
</head>

<body>
    {% include header.liquid %}

    <main id="main-content" class="fpl-wrap">

        <section class="fpl-hero">
            {%- if fplPicks.size > 0 -%}<p class="fpl-status">Live, updated every gameweek</p>{%- else -%}<p class="fpl-status">Coming soon</p>{%- endif -%}
            <h1>An AI picks a Fantasy Premier League team, every gameweek</h1>
            <p class="fpl-lede">
                This page will show the squad an AI has chosen for the 2026/27 season: the starting
                eleven in formation, the captain, the chip plan, and the reasoning behind every
                decision. Published before each deadline, never after the results are in.
            </p>
            <p class="fpl-when">
                First picks go live before the opening deadline, <strong>Friday 21 August 2026, 18:30 BST</strong>.
                <span class="fpl-countdown" data-fpl-countdown="2026-08-21T17:30:00Z"></span>
            </p>
            <div class="fpl-cta">
                <a class="fpl-btn" href="#join">Join the free league</a>
                <a class="fpl-btn fpl-btn-ghost" href="/blog/ai-fantasy-premier-league-experiment/">Read how it works</a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="fpl-section">
            <h2>What will be on this page</h2>
            <p>
                Once the season starts, this becomes the live view of the team. Four things, updated
                every gameweek.
            </p>
            <ul class="fpl-grid">
                <li class="fpl-panel">
                    <h3>The starting eleven</h3>
                    <p>The full squad in a formation view, with the bench in order and the captain and vice marked.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="fpl-panel">
                    <h3>The captain call</h3>
                    <p>Who is taking the armband and why, including when the model goes for a differential over the obvious premium.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="fpl-panel">
                    <h3>The reasoning</h3>
                    <p>Every transfer explained. Who came in, who went out, and what the numbers said at the time.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="fpl-panel">
                    <h3>The chip plan</h3>
                    <p>Triple Captain, Bench Boost, Free Hit and Wildcard, called in advance and aimed at double gameweeks.</p>
                </li>
            </ul>

{%- assign latest = fplPicks | last -%}
            {%- if latest -%}
            {%- assign week = latest -%}
            {% include fpl-xi.liquid %}
            {%- if fplPicks.size > 1 -%}
            <p class="fpl-team-foot">Earlier gameweeks: 
                {%- for w in fplPicks reversed -%}
                {%- unless forloop.first %} {% endunless -%}
                <a href="/fpl/gameweek-{{ w.gameweek }}/">GW{{ w.gameweek }}</a>{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
                {%- endfor -%}
            </p>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- else -%}
            <div class="fpl-pitch" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="fpl-row"><span class="fpl-slot"></span></div>
                <div class="fpl-row"><span class="fpl-slot"></span><span class="fpl-slot"></span><span class="fpl-slot"></span><span class="fpl-slot"></span></div>
                <div class="fpl-row"><span class="fpl-slot"></span><span class="fpl-slot"></span><span class="fpl-slot"></span><span class="fpl-slot"></span></div>
                <div class="fpl-row"><span class="fpl-slot"></span><span class="fpl-slot"></span></div>
            </div>
            <p class="fpl-pitch-note">An empty formation. The real eleven appears here from 21 August.</p>
            {%- endif -%}
        </section>

        <section class="fpl-section">
            <h2>How the AI decides</h2>
            <p>
                The base is unemotional. Models do not make the eleven o'clock Sunday transfer, do not
                captain out of spite, and do not burn a chip because three red arrows felt like a crisis.
                That alone removes most of what ruins a human season.
            </p>
            <p>
                But purely sensible models converge on the template and finish forgettably, because
                Fantasy Premier League rewards being right when everyone else was wrong. So this one has
                explicit permission to be brave: differential captains when the upside justifies it, and
                chips timed for double gameweeks rather than hoarded until the fixtures run out.
            </p>
            <p>
                The full argument, including the honest bit about how these experiments usually go, is in
                <a href="/blog/ai-fantasy-premier-league-experiment/">the launch post</a>.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="fpl-section">
            <h2>The data behind the picks</h2>
            <p>
                All public, all credited. Nothing proprietary and nothing scraped from anywhere it should
                not be.
            </p>
            <dl class="fpl-sources">
                <div>
                    <dt>Core FPL scoring, minutes, cards, bonus, prices and ownership</dt>
                    <dd><a href="https://fantasy.premierleague.com/api/bootstrap-static/" rel="noopener">Official FPL API</a>, which also carries Opta expected goals and an official injury flag, plus <a href="https://github.com/vaastav/Fantasy-Premier-League" rel="noopener">Vaastav's historical dataset</a> for earlier seasons</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Player-level expected goals outside the Premier League</dt>
                    <dd><a href="https://understat.com" rel="noopener">Understat</a>, covering the big five European leagues</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Results history, home and away splits, odds and referees</dt>
                    <dd><a href="https://www.football-data.co.uk" rel="noopener">Football-Data.co.uk</a></dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Team strength</dt>
                    <dd><a href="http://clubelo.com" rel="noopener">ClubElo</a> ratings</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Weather at each ground</dt>
                    <dd><a href="https://open-meteo.com" rel="noopener">Open-Meteo</a>, called at prediction time</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Fixtures, including televised reschedules</dt>
                    <dd><a href="https://pl.ecal.com" rel="noopener">Official Premier League calendar</a></dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Also weighted</dt>
                    <dd>Fixture difficulty and congestion, referee card tendencies, and per-league conversion factors, because a forty goal Ligue 1 striker is not a forty goal Premier League striker.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Deliberately not used</dt>
                    <dd>Transfermarkt bars automated extraction and FBref restricts scraping, so both are out. Fantasy Football Scout, Fantasy Football Hub and FootyStats are subscriptions, and this runs on sources anyone can check for free. The cost is no predicted lineups, so rotation risk is derived from starts and the official availability flag instead, and promoted club players are judged on shot volume rather than shot quality.</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
        </section>

        <section class="fpl-section" id="join">
            <h2>Join the league and beat it</h2>
            <p>
                The league is <strong>Algorithm By Coffee &amp; Fun LLC</strong>, a free invitational
                classic league. It is open now.
            </p>

            <div class="fpl-join">
                <div class="fpl-code-row">
                    <span class="fpl-code" data-fpl-code>bsg8nz</span>
                    <button type="button" class="fpl-copy" data-fpl-copy="bsg8nz" hidden>Copy code</button>
                    <span class="fpl-copied" data-fpl-copied role="status"></span>
                </div>
                <ol class="fpl-steps">
                    <li>Log in to Fantasy Premier League.</li>
                    <li>Go to <strong>Leagues</strong>, then <strong>Join a league</strong>.</li>
                    <li>Enter the code <strong>bsg8nz</strong>.</li>
                </ol>
                <p class="fpl-free">
                    No entry fee, no prizes, nothing to buy. Charging to enter a competition raises
                    gambling and prize competition law questions, so a paid league was ruled out on
                    purpose. Bragging rights only.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="fpl-section">
            <h2>Questions</h2>
            <div class="fpl-faq">
                <details>
                    <summary>When do the picks go live?</summary>
                    <div>
                        <p>The first squad is published before the opening deadline of the 2026/27 season, which is Friday 21 August 2026 at 18:30 BST. The season opens that evening with Arsenal against Coventry, not on the Saturday. After that a new set of picks goes up every gameweek, along with the reasoning.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>Is the league free to join?</summary>
                    <div>
                        <p>Yes. No entry fee and no prizes. Charging people to enter a competition walks into gambling and prize competition law, so it was ruled out deliberately in favour of bragging rights.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>Can I join after the season has started?</summary>
                    <div>
                        <p>Yes. Classic leagues can be joined at any point. Your league score counts from the gameweek you join onward, so joining in November means competing with fewer points banked.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>What data does the AI use?</summary>
                    <div>
                        <p>Free public data only, listed and linked in full above. The FPL API does most of the work, including Opta expected goals and official injury status. Understat adds player-level expected goals for the big five European leagues, Football-Data.co.uk supplies results, odds and referees, ClubElo the team strength ratings and Open-Meteo the weather.</p>
                        <p>It gets no insider information and no eye test. It sees numbers, and occasionally that will be an expensive limitation.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>Will the bad weeks be published too?</summary>
                    <div>
                        <p>Yes, written up identically to the good ones, with no quiet deletions. That is the entire premise. A transparency project that only publishes the wins is just marketing.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>Is this betting advice?</summary>
                    <div>
                        <p>No. It is a free fantasy football experiment run for fun by one person, and no money changes hands at any point.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>Is this affiliated with the Premier League?</summary>
                    <div>
                        <p>No. This is an independent project by Coffee &amp; Fun LLC. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to the Premier League or the official Fantasy Premier League game.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>
            </div>
        </section>

    </main>

    {% include modals.liquid %}
    {% include footer.liquid %}

    {% pageJs "fpl" %}
</body>
</html>
